PROD-003 (notepad product templates) is implemented on branch
feat/PROD-003-notepads — check `gh pr list` before assuming it's merged.

What it added, and the two things worth knowing before touching products:
- A 'notepad' category with seven rectangular presets and a custom size, and
  a new per-category property: how the trim line is MARKED. Pins and magnets
  are cut out one at a time, so they keep their dashed outline; pads are
  guillotined, so they get corner crop marks (productMarks / PRODUCT_MARKS,
  carried on ProductGuideSpec.marks — optional, so designs saved before pads
  keep the old behaviour).
- Imposition now differs by mark style, which is the load-bearing bit:
  * 'outline' products keep PROD-001's layout — every copy carries its own
    bleed, inside the sheet's printer margin.
  * 'corner' products tile the sheet edge to edge at TRIM size: neighbours
    share one cut line and the sheet's outer edges (margin and all) are
    trimmed off the finished pad. Without this an A6 pad ganged one per
    sheet, which is no ganging at all.
  * Capacity also tries the product turned a quarter and keeps whichever
    gangs more (`rotated` on the layout). Half-letter on Letter and A5 on A4
    only reach their classic two-up that way. Anything that draws a cell —
    screen guides, export marks, cell size — has to swap its axes when
    `sheet.rotated` is set; three places do, and all three have tests.
- A custom product's shape is now derived (defaultShape) when the category
  doesn't offer a choice: the shape control is per-category and its state
  persisted, so a custom pad used to inherit "circle" from a magnet.

Known trade-off, deliberate and stated in the setup panel: tiling to the
sheet edge means a home printer's unprintable margin is inside the trimmed-off
border, so the outermost pads lose a sliver unless printed on a press.

